Subject: [PATCH] OnePlus 11 (salami) mainline enablement
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This series brings up the OnePlus 11 (codename "salami", SM8550) on
mainline Linux, on top of v7.3-rc merge base 5fc5768c7ca9.

It adds the device tree and defconfig, the Samsung AMB670YF07/YF08 DSI
panel driver, the Synaptics TouchComm I2C touchscreen driver, an
IST8801 hall sensor driver and a Qualcomm bootloader log driver, plus
the small core hacks still needed downstream (appended DTB support,
PCIe/ath12k fixes).

ynk (11):
  arm64: boot: Add support for appended device tree blob
  drm/panel: Add Samsung AMB670YF07 DSI panel driver
  arm64: dts: qcom: Add OnePlus 11 (salami) device tree and defconfig
  soc: qcom: Add bootloader log driver
  arm64: dts: qcom: salami: Add power key and disable LOCALVERSION_AUTO
  Input: Add Synaptics TouchComm I2C touchscreen driver
  drm/panel: Add Samsung AMB670YF07/YF08 panel driver
  arm64: configs: salami: Trim defconfig and build key drivers in
  PCI: qcom: Fix ath12k WiFi bring-up on SM8550
  arm64: configs: salami: Set kernel command line and enable PAS
  arm64: dts: qcom: salami: Add audio, hall sensor and cache properties

